title: 'pallet-scheduler: remove aborted and unserviceable tasks from agendas'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Makes agenda servicing in `pallet-scheduler` more robust.

    Tasks aborted with `CallUnavailable` or `PermanentlyOverweight` are now removed from their
    agenda together with their name and retry configuration.

    A due task whose call is a preimage lookup longer than `Preimages::MAX_LENGTH` can never be
    fetched. It is now removed with `CallUnavailable` and charged only for its cleanup. Every other
    task whose service does not fit is still postponed, whatever `MaximumWeight` is set to.

    `MaximumWeight` should cover servicing a lookup of `Preimages::MAX_LENGTH` as the first task of
    a full agenda, and leave enough of the maximum block weight for the work done before the
    scheduler runs.

    The weight budget of a block is treated as fresh only until the first task is serviced.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    `CallUnavailable` and `PermanentlyOverweight` now mean that the task was removed from storage:
    it will not run, and cancelling, rescheduling or setting a retry configuration for it by
    address returns `NotFound`. Indexers and governance UIs that track scheduled tasks or
    enactments can treat both events as final.

    Lowering `MaximumWeight` postpones the tasks whose service no longer fits, as before. A task
    whose call itself is heavier than the new value is still reported as `PermanentlyOverweight`,
    as before, and is now removed rather than left unreachable in its agenda.
crates:
- name: pallet-scheduler
  bump: patch
